[CENTER]
[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#E74C3C]R[/COLOR][COLOR=#F39C12]T[/COLOR][COLOR=#27AE60]P[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#7F8C8D]Random Teleport — the RTP engine[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[I]Send your players to a safe, random spot in the world — fast, fair, and designed not to lag your server.[/I]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#27AE60][B]Free.[/B][/COLOR] [B]RTP-Pro[/B] is an optional upgrade for Folia, multi-server / proxy networks, claim-plugin integrations, and priority support.[/SIZE]

[URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP'][IMG]https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/dailystruggle/RTP?label=Version&style=for-the-badge&color=2C3E50[/IMG][/URL] [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP'][IMG]https://img.shields.io/github/license/dailystruggle/RTP?label=License&style=for-the-badge&color=2C3E50[/IMG][/URL]
[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Why RTP?[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Random teleportation looks cheap and easy, but it is one of the most resource-intensive tasks on a Minecraft server: chunk loading, safe-placement checks, re-rolling, and players still wandering off afterwards. RTP was built to solve [I]all[/I] of that on the same plugin:

[LIST]
[*]🌀 [B]Spiral-based selection[/B] — bounded math instead of unbounded re-roll loops. Selection time stays predictable even on huge worlds.
[*]🧠 [B]Spatial memory[/B] — RTP [I]learns[/I] which sectors keep failing and stops trying them. Selection gets faster the longer the server runs.
[*]⏱️ [B]Pre-generated queue[/B] — most of the time there's already a verified destination ready before the player even types `/rtp`.
[*]🛡️ [B]Safe placement[/B] — configurable safety radius, optional landing platform, invulnerability timer, flat material allow/deny list.
[*]🌍 [B]Per-region, per-world configuration[/B] — square or circle, weighted curves, vertical bounds, optional sky-light check, world overrides.
[*]🔌 [B]Works with the plugins you already run[/B] — PlaceholderAPI, ProtocolLib. ([I]Vault economy and claim-plugin integrations are an [B]RTP-Pro[/B] feature.[/I])
[/LIST]

[CENTER][I]Originally published as [URL='https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/rtp.94812/']RTP 2.x[/URL] — this resource is the successor on the rewritten 3.0 engine.[/I][/CENTER]

[CENTER][COLOR=#D1D1D1]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#16A085]Quick Start[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop the `RTP-x.y.z.jar` into your server's `plugins/` folder.
[*]Start (or restart) the server. Default config and a `default` region are generated automatically.
[*]Type [B]`/rtp`[/B] in-game.
[/LIST]

That's it for the smoke test. Tweak `plugins/RTP/config.yml` and `plugins/RTP/regions/*.yml` once you want per-region radii, biomes, or weighting.

